Snapshot: ghost-robot still-grid baseline, 2026-09-25 — port vs the
Ghost Robot C oracle on the shared still matrix: 32/288 cells
byte-identical; control run under mainline-4.2.0 is 288/288.

This is the phase-3.1 baseline of docs/PLAN-ORACLES-AND-CLEANUP.md: the
per-cell divergence map the phase-3.2 ports are measured against. A
dated record — re-measure rather than reading this as current state.

host:    i265 (Core Ultra 7 265K, 20 threads / 30 GB; run-heavy --mem 8G --jobs 6)
oracle:  ghost-robot = reference/svt-av1-hdr @ 9dabe3ca04390e2e19267bf87a48c6cab44d6111
         ("Ghost Robot" = mainline v4.2.0 + 144 master + 73 fork commits)
control: mainline-4.2.0 = reference/svt-av1 @ 9292ec8e32bce26f781f277ec8739b53426c4300
port:    893f6823 (Ghost Robot defaults: HdrForkConfig::ghost_robot(),
         reference-keyed resolution — plan 1.3) plus the docs tick.
command: tools/oracle_still_grid.sh <oracle> <out.tsv>
         (exports SVT_ORACLE; each cell runs tools/identity_diff.sh, which
         drives both encoders on the one .yuv and reports the first
         divergent tile op + stage)
grid:    contents {gradient, photo=crop:CID22-512/training/1001682.png}
         x sizes {64,128,256} x bd {8,10} x qp {20,32,45,55}
         x presets {2,4,6,8,10,13} = 288 cells/oracle.
data:    benchmarks/ghost_robot_baseline_2026-09-25.{ghost-robot,mainline-4.2.0}.tsv

ghost-robot: 32 / 288 IDENTICAL

  by content   gradient 28/144   photo 4/144
